---
/**
 * SiteMark — the way home from anywhere.
 *
 * The drawing is `MarkGlyph.astro`; this file is where it sits, how big it is,
 * and what pressing it does. The two were one component until `/design` needed
 * to render the same lockup as a specimen, at which point the glyph moved to its
 * own file rather than being copied. What is left here is everything that is
 * true of the mark *as a fixed control* and of nothing else.
 *
 * **20px below 900px, 24px above.** The lockup is 2.06 ink widths where the A
 * alone was one, and below 900px the mark has to stay inside the
 * `--page-pad + 2.5rem` strip the shell already clears for the vertical MENU
 * label: 40px of it at 375px, 33.4px of which is ink. It sits at
 * `left: var(--page-pad)` there, so the page scrolls past to the right of it
 * rather than underneath it; above 900px it moves to the rail's own left edge,
 * so mark and dashes share a column.
 *
 * **The left bearing is 0.096 of the mark's height, and adding the M did not
 * move it.** The leftmost ink is the outer corner of the A's left foot, 1.5366
 * of 16 units, so the negative margin lines the *ink* up with the rail instead
 * of the box. Measured delta from the A-only mark: 0.008px.
 *
 * Layer 50: above the rail (40) and below the mobile trigger (60) and everything
 * modal, so an open nav panel or palette covers the mark rather than fighting it.
 */
import MarkGlyph from "./MarkGlyph.astro";
---

{/*
  No `aria-current` on home. The rail's Home dash already carries it, and two
  "current page" announcements for one destination is noise, not redundancy.

  The glyph takes no label: this anchor is already named "Home", and naming the
  drawing as well would read the letters out after it.

  `data-mnav-inert`: the open MENU panel covers this anchor (layer 80 over 50),
  so it goes inert with the rest of the background — a focusable control behind
  a modal is a stop the keyboard can reach and the eye cannot. The wiring is
  `MobileNav.astro › setOpen`; `lib/mnav.test.mjs` holds it.
*/}
<a class="mark press" href="/" aria-label="Home" data-mnav-inert>
  <MarkGlyph />
</a>

<style>
  .mark {
    /* Read by `MarkGlyph.astro`, which sets its height from it. */
    --mark-size: 20px;

    /* Optical, and the same correction the masthead makes with its -0.04em:
       line up the ink, not the box. 1.5366 units of 16 = 9.6% of the mark's
       height, so a box flush with the rail would put the letter 2px inboard of
       the dashes under it. */
    margin-left: calc(var(--mark-size) * -0.096);

    position: fixed;
    top: clamp(1.25rem, 3.5vh, 2rem);
    /* Below 900px the shell clears `--page-pad + 2.5rem` on the left for the
       vertical MENU label. Sitting inside that strip is what keeps the mark out
       of the content column, and the MENU label is at the vertical middle, so
       the two never meet. */
    left: var(--page-pad);
    z-index: 50;
    display: block;
    color: var(--fg);
  }

  @media (min-width: 900px) {
    .mark {
      --mark-size: 24px;
      /* The rail's own left edge. Mark and dashes share a column. */
      left: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2.75rem);
    }
  }

  .mark:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* A 40px hit area without a 40px layout box, the same `::before` trick the
     rail dashes use — the glyph stays exactly where `left` puts it. The vertical
     padding is derived rather than typed, so the 40px floor holds at both mark
     sizes without a second number to keep in step. */
  .mark::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: calc((40px - var(--mark-size)) / -2) -8px;
  }
</style>
